      ":question/id": "9a832124-e7c1-5d36-a8d7-a22e220546d7",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-126535",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $F(x,y)=(3{x}^{2}-y)\\,i+(2x+{y}^{3})\\,j,$ what is the scalar curl of $F?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x+{y}^{3})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}-y) \\\\  & =2-(-1) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
