      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-126547",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $F(x,y)={y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)\\,i+({x}^{2}-y)\\,j,$ what is the scalar curl of $F?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-y)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)) \\\\  & =2x-2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"
