      ":question/id": "5ab1d5d9-c180-5acc-b2cc-0f6200926992",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-131348",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=({x}^{2}+xy)\\,i+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,j.$ Evaluate the scalar curl of $F$ at the point $(\\frac{1}{2},0).$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y))-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+xy) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x+y}-x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the scalar curl at the point $(\\frac{1}{2},0),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})}_{(1/2,0)} & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{2}+0)}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
