      ":question/problem": "Given that $F(x,y)=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,i+\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,j,$ what is the scalar curl of $F?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    }
  ],
  ":knowledge-point/title": "Calculating the Scalar Curl of a Vector Field"
}
